diff --git a/debian/changelog b/debian/changelog
index c0bf082..32e8ad8 100644
--- a/debian/changelog
+++ b/debian/changelog
@@ -1,3 +1,32 @@
+python-escript (6.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium
+
+  * New upstream release (6.1.1).
+  * d/sid_options.py: enable HDF5 (serial) alongside NetCDF; esys-escript 6.x
+    supports both. Add libhdf5-dev to Build-Depends (NetCDF kept).
+  * Enable mpi4py in the MPI build: d/sid_options_mpi.py sets mpi4py=True; add
+    python3-mpi4py to Build-Depends and to python3-escript-mpi Depends. The
+    user guide documents it (mpi4py chapter).
+  * Refer to the project as esys-escript in the package descriptions.
+  * Drop references to the esys.downunder module and its inversion guide; the
+    module was removed upstream in 6.x (d/control, d/python-escript-doc.install,
+    remove d/python-escript-doc.doc-base.4).
+  * python-escript-doc: reconcile to the 6.x doc set. Ship the Sphinx Python API
+    HTML (python_html). Drop the cookbook and install PDFs and their doc-base
+    entries (cookbook.tex/install.tex removed upstream; the install guide is now
+    installation.md, shipped as-is). Keep user guide (PDF), C++ API (Doxygen) and
+    Python API (Sphinx). esys-escript naming in the doc-base titles.
+  * Bump Standards-Version to 4.7.2 (no changes needed).
+  * d/patches: drop 8 obsolete patches (32bitboostextract, enable-silo,
+    mpi-multiarch — the targeted scons/templates/sid_options.py is now an
+    unused wrapper; make — no top-level Makefile; g++10-fix — upstreamed;
+    boost_numpy — probe rewritten upstream; tex — the LaTeX FTBFS refs are
+    fixed upstream; py3 — 6.x is py3-native). Rebase py3.13, use-t1-encoding,
+    which (run-escript only; the gmsh which-block was removed upstream) and
+    fix-dpkg-buildflags against the 6.1.x source. The full series applies
+    cleanly to the new source (build/lintian validation still TODO).
+
+ -- Lutz Gross <lutz.gross@gmail.com>  Tue, 09 Jun 2026 19:02:15 +1000
+
 python-escript (5.6-10) unstable; urgency=medium
 
   * Team upload.
